# The code owner of the files that decide what CI checks.
#
# The CI job `lean` runs the audit files of the pull request itself. Thus
# a pull request that weakens them passes its own weaker audit. Cesar
# Canassa, the repository owner, decided on 2026-10-16 (dashboard question
# `lean-ci-q1`) that a change to these files needs his review. The rule
# takes effect only when the ruleset on master has "Require review from
# Code Owners" on.
#
# `/.github/` includes this file and every workflow, so the guard `check`
# and the job `lean` cannot change without that review. `.gitattributes`
# has no leading `/`, so it matches that file in every directory: its
# `export-ignore` removes a file from the export of scripts/audit.sh
# (#262).
#
# The proof sources are not listed. The audit checks axioms, `sorry`,
# commands and the kernel, not what a theorem states, so a review of a
# proof pull request must check the statements.

/proofs/ownership/Axioms.lean        @canassa
/proofs/ownership/Audit.lean         @canassa
/proofs/ownership/lakefile.toml      @canassa
/proofs/ownership/lake-manifest.json @canassa
/proofs/ownership/lean-toolchain     @canassa
/proofs/ownership/scripts/           @canassa
/flake.nix                           @canassa
/flake.lock                          @canassa
/.github/                            @canassa
.gitattributes                       @canassa
